# The Status tab answering "why is this not working".
#
# Everything above the fold on this screen describes traffic: packets in, packets out, airtime.
# None of it can explain a send that the radio refused before it ever transmitted, or a
# firmware decision the user is supposed to know about. These three rows are those answers.

scene demo
tab status

# A busy queue is worth a row; an idle one is not, so the row appears here rather than always.
queue 6 16

# The radio refusing a packet outright. No Routing reply will ever arrive for it, so this row
# and the message's own "!!" are the whole of the report.
queue 0 16 refused
hold 900

# The firmware explaining itself, at the level it chose.
notice warn Duty cycle limit reached, transmit paused
hold 900
notice error Channel key mismatch on LongFast
hold 900

# And a radio that keeps restarting under a link that survives it.
reboots 3
hold 1200
